# The vendored dependency snapshots must ship their compiled `dist/` output —
# that is the runtime JavaScript the client loads. The repository-root `dist/`
# rule is unanchored, so it would otherwise drop every vendored package's
# build output. `apps/electron/dist` (this package's own build directory)
# stays ignored through the root rule.
!vendor/**/dist/
!vendor/**/dist/**
# Nested dependency copies inside a vendored package are part of the shipped
# resolution order (Node resolves them before the top-level copy), so they ship
# as well. `apps/electron/node_modules` stays ignored through the root rule.
!vendor/**/node_modules/
!vendor/**/node_modules/**
